      {
        "id": "thm-weak-lq-sample-covariance-entrywise-deviation",
        "kind": "theorem",
        "title": "Entrywise deviation for sample-centered covariance under directional Gaussian tails",
        "statement": "Let $X_1,\\ldots,X_n$ be iid from $\\mathcal P_q(\\tau,c_{n,p})$ of [[def-weak-lq-sparse-covariance-class]], with $n\\ge1$, $p\\ge2$, and $\\tau>0$. Let $u>0$ and let $\\widehat\\Sigma^\\ast$ be the sample-centered covariance. Then\n$$\\mathbb P\\!\\left(\\max_{1\\le j,k\\le p}|\\widehat\\sigma^\\ast_{jk}-\\sigma_{jk}|\n\\le192\\tau\\left(\\sqrt{\\frac un}+\\frac un\\right)\\right)\\ge1-2pe^{-u}-2p^2e^{-2u}.$$\nIn particular $u=\\log(8p^4)$ gives the original probability $1-p^{-2}$.\nNo independence between coordinates of a single observation is assumed.",
        "deps": [
