        "kind": "lemma",
        "title": "Diagonal covariance lower bound with bounded-risk saturation",
        "statement": "Assume AC, as inherited through [[thm-fano-packing]]. For every $n\\ge1$,\n$p\\ge2$, $\\tau>0$, $0\\le q<1$ and $c\\ge0$, the minimax squared operator\nrisk of [[def-minimax-squared-operator-risk]] over\n$\\mathcal P_q(\\tau,c)$ of [[def-weak-lq-sparse-covariance-class]] satisfies\n$$\\mathfrak R_n(\\mathcal P_q(\\tau,c))\\ge b\\tau^2\\min\\{1,\\log(p)/n\\},$$\nfor an absolute constant $b>0$. In particular, the lower bound applies when\n$c=0$ and when an effective sparse-row count rounds to zero.",
